{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Wound</b> — that blood issues from them." "<b>Cleansing</b> — like תמרוקיה, מרקו הרמחים, מורק ושוטף, and its pattern is like תגמול. That is: just as the glory of young men is their strength, and the old men's gray hair is their glory that others honor, so bruises of a wound are a glory to be a cleansing in a wicked man, to remove his evils; and likewise blows that reach the chambers of the belly — they are the cleansings of evil."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:52.882687681Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}